  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. When `clamp=True` and the range had an open bound (`min_open` or `max_open`), the clamped value landed outside the allowed range. For example, `IntRange(0, min_open=True, clamp=True)` turned `-5` into `-1`. The code moved away from the bound (`bound - dir`) instead of into the range (`bound + dir`). It now gives `1`.\n\nI added two cases to the clamp tests in `tests/test_types.py`: `-5` clamps to `1` with `min_open`, and `9` clamps to `4` with `max_open` and a max of 5. `tests/test_types.py` passes (43 passed, 2 skipped). I didn't run the full suite.",
